1
00:00:01,584 --> 00:00:03,002
<i>Are we okay?</i>

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:04,838
<i>What do you mean?</i>

3
00:00:04,921 --> 00:00:06,840
<i>There's something you're not telling me.</i>

4
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:09,592
[SCOFFS] <i>I'll admit it.</i>

5
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:12,178
<i>Dude, I…</i>

6
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:15,181
<i>I'm in love with you.</i>

7
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:21,229
<i>Jordan, say something.</i>

8
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:24,149
<i>Huh?</i>

9
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:28,153
<i>Is there any way we can lower the cost</i>

10
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:31,322
<i>of the additional security measures</i>
<i>you proposed?</i>

11
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:32,532
<i>That's all?</i>

12
00:00:32,615 --> 00:00:33,658
[CHUCKLES]

13
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:34,617
<i>I thought…</i>

14
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:36,619
<i>Thought what?</i>

15
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:37,996
<i>Nothing.</i>

16
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:40,874
<i>Um, okay. I'll review it again.</i>

17
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:45,712
<i>Good night.</i>

18
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:48,548
<i>Good night.</i>

19
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:54,888
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

20
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:56,222
<i>Ralph.</i>

21
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:58,683
<i>I-I just want to…</i>

22
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:01,227
<i>I just need to talk to you about Charm.</i>

23
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,395
<i>So,</i>

24
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:06,274
<i>are you here because you're</i>
<i>finally breaking up with her?</i>

25
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:07,734
<i>No.</i>

26
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:11,696
<i>She's the one breaking up with me.</i>

27
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,324
<i>She's willing to let me go</i>

28
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:17,368
<i>just so I can make up with you.</i>

29
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:19,954
<i>I'm sorry, son.</i>

30
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:23,249
[BILLY] <i>Ralph.</i>

31
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:25,376
<i>You may want to add something?</i>

32
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:28,963
<i>Because if you've set your mind</i>
<i>on something,</i>

33
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:32,467
<i>you don't wait for the perfect time.</i>

34
00:01:33,635 --> 00:01:35,178
<i>You choose the moment.</i>

35
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:39,766
[EXHALES DEEPLY]
<i>Okay. Um…</i>

36
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:43,269
<i>What I'm trying to say is</i>

37
00:01:43,353 --> 00:01:44,479
<i>that even if…</i>

38
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:48,983
<i>a lot of people are against us,</i>

39
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:51,277
<i>Charm…</i>

40
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:56,324
<i>will you marry me?</i>

41
00:01:57,617 --> 00:01:59,410
<i>Didn't I tell you</i>

42
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:02,372
<i>to fix your relationship</i>
<i>with your mom first?</i>

43
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:05,416
<i>Babe, that's more important.</i>

44
00:02:08,461 --> 00:02:11,297
<i>I'll be the happiest</i>
<i>if you will say yes, dear.</i>

45
00:02:11,381 --> 00:02:14,050
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

46
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:15,760
<i>My son said that</i>

47
00:02:16,427 --> 00:02:20,557
<i>you're willing to let him go</i>
<i>just so that he can fix our relationship.</i>

48
00:02:21,432 --> 00:02:22,433
<i>And Billy,</i>

49
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:25,270
<i>you never stopped telling my son</i>
<i>to always reach out to me.</i>

50
00:02:25,937 --> 00:02:26,938
<i>Thank you.</i>

51
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,482
<i>Charm, I'm so sorry.</i>

52
00:02:32,026 --> 00:02:35,363
<i>Ralph, what are you waiting for?</i>
<i>Ask her again.</i>

53
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:38,783
<i>- Uh, Charm.</i>
<i>- Mm?</i>

54
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:39,784
<i>Babe?</i>

55
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:42,328
<i>Will you marry me?</i>

56
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:43,329
<i>- Yes!</i>
- [RALPH CHUCKLES]

57
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:45,665
<i>- Of course, yes!</i>
- [STAFF CHEER]

58
00:02:45,748 --> 00:02:46,708
<i>Oh my God!</i>

59
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,376
[ROWENA] <i>Wow.</i>

60
00:02:50,253 --> 00:02:54,048
[LUCY]<i> How's the search</i>
<i>for your other family?</i>

61
00:02:54,132 --> 00:02:55,842
[ENRICO]
<i>I go to her grave once in a while,</i>

62
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:59,888
<i>hoping that her mom</i>
<i>and sister would visit,</i>

63
00:03:00,471 --> 00:03:01,431
<i>but…</i>

64
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:05,435
[LUCY] <i>And you found Billy's family first.</i>

65
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:09,981
<i>Does Billy know that</i>

66
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:12,483
<i>she has siblings other than Oliver?</i>

67
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:15,111
<i>I don't know how to tell her.</i>

68
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:17,405
<i>If I were you, I'd tell her everything.</i>

69
00:03:17,488 --> 00:03:19,282
<i>Sure, she's going to get hurt,</i>

70
00:03:19,365 --> 00:03:21,659
<i>but that's better than</i>
<i>lying to her forever.</i>

71
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:23,912
- [ENRICO] Where--
- There's a fight!

72
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:25,288
- Auntie…
- [ENRICO] Wait up!

73
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:26,873
- Hurry up!
- Calm down.

74
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:27,874
Hurry!

75
00:03:28,374 --> 00:03:29,208
Why--

76
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:31,920
- [SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]
- [ENRICO EXHALES]

77
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,130
- Ta-da!
- [BILLY CLEARS THROAT]

78
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:36,633
Did you think we forgot?

79
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:38,092
[OLIVER CLAPPING]

80
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:39,928
Happy birthday.

81
00:03:40,011 --> 00:03:43,932
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

82
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,308
Happy birthday, Dad.

83
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:47,393
[OLIVER] Make a wish! Make a wish!

84
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:49,187
[OLIVER] Boom!

85
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:52,440
[CHUCKLES]

86
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:53,566
Thank you.

87
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:58,655
I'll take you
to Billy's favorite restaurant.

88
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:00,323
They serve seafood there.

89
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:01,783
Do you like seafood?

90
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:03,868
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

91
00:04:03,952 --> 00:04:05,662
- Okay. Let's go, Auntie Pres?
- [PRECIOUS] Mm.

92
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:09,040
- Okay, let's bring this.
- Let's box it up.

93
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:10,875
Happy birthday, Pa.

94
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:15,797
I'll check your wound, Ma.

95
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:20,551
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:04:21,177 --> 00:04:22,345
Tsk.

97
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:26,724
We need to have the doctor
check on it again.

98
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:29,978
I want to leave.

99
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:33,064
I can't take it anymore.

100
00:04:34,148 --> 00:04:35,316
Ma…

101
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:45,243
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

102
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:53,042
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

103
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:34,208
[PLATES, CUTLERY CLINKING]

104
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:35,168
Pa.

105
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:39,714
What did you wish for earlier?

106
00:05:39,797 --> 00:05:45,970
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:48,598
<i>I'm Private Investigator Jimenez.</i>

108
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:50,516
<i>Uh…</i>

109
00:05:51,267 --> 00:05:53,269
<i>Have you found my wife and daughters?</i>

110
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:56,314
<i>I'm afraid I have some bad news.</i>

111
00:05:57,356 --> 00:06:00,610
<i>Your eldest daughter, Abigail?</i>

112
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:06,741
[JIMENEZ] <i>She died in a fire.</i>

113
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:09,994
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

114
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:13,289
FIRE BURNS DOWN HOME

115
00:06:13,372 --> 00:06:14,707
[ENRICO] <i>Abi, dear…</i>

116
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:18,169
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

117
00:06:18,961 --> 00:06:22,006
<i>I wasn't a good father to you and Bea.</i>

118
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:25,968
<i>I promise…</i>

119
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:31,015
<i>I will find your mother and sister.</i>

120
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:33,351
<i>I don't know if Billy will ever</i>
<i>be able to forgive me</i>

121
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:35,186
<i>for what I'm about to tell her.</i>

122
00:06:35,269 --> 00:06:37,355
<i>I know this is too much.</i>

123
00:06:37,438 --> 00:06:40,149
<i>But she needs to know the truth.</i>

124
00:06:41,734 --> 00:06:47,824
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

125
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:49,492
I wished that…

126
00:06:52,161 --> 00:06:53,579
That…

127
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,083
[PRECIOUS] Enrico?

128
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:00,044
Are you okay?

129
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:03,714
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,758
I wished that we'd always be like this.

131
00:07:07,051 --> 00:07:08,469
Happy

132
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:11,431
and all together.

133
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:13,850
[OLIVER] Of course, Papa.

134
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:15,810
We won't be apart anymore.

135
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:17,979
Right, Billy?

136
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:20,398
Yes, that's right.

137
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:24,652
We're finally complete.

138
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:31,033
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

139
00:07:39,834 --> 00:07:45,381
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

140
00:07:49,635 --> 00:07:51,220
[MUSIC FADES]

141
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:57,143
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

142
00:08:00,438 --> 00:08:04,275
[BUSY TONE]

143
00:08:09,614 --> 00:08:12,158
- [BUSY TONE]
- [KNOCKING ON DOOR]

144
00:08:12,241 --> 00:08:13,367
- Enrico?
- Oh.

145
00:08:14,535 --> 00:08:15,453
Uh…

146
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:18,706
Why are you still up?

147
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:22,043
I'm just finishing up doing
the canteen's inventory.

148
00:08:22,126 --> 00:08:23,085
Hmm.

149
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:26,339
Enrico, are you really okay?

150
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:28,007
Billy and I noticed earlier

151
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:30,301
that you seemed to have something
weighing on your mind.

152
00:08:30,384 --> 00:08:31,677
Is something bothering you?

153
00:08:33,846 --> 00:08:35,473
Auntie Pres…

154
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,475
Oh. Sorry, sorry.

155
00:08:37,558 --> 00:08:39,810
I'll go now. Go to bed too.

156
00:08:40,394 --> 00:08:41,479
Okay.

157
00:08:43,314 --> 00:08:49,570
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

158
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:56,452
[BILLY'S LAWYER]<i> The other</i>
<i>party is relentless.</i>

159
00:08:56,536 --> 00:09:00,289
<i>They don't want to say why</i>
<i>they're mad at you.</i>

160
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:04,794
<i>I can't think of any reason, Attorney.</i>

161
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:08,756
There are cases of
targeted harassment, Billy.

162
00:09:08,839 --> 00:09:11,092
Sometimes,
they don't have any clear motive.

163
00:09:11,175 --> 00:09:12,718
It's just because of obsession.

164
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:15,555
Attorney, I just want you to reassure me

165
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:19,684
that Bea can't do anything else
to help herself and her mother.

166
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,727
<i>We're doing everything that we can.</i>

167
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:23,688
<i>But we cannot stop the process.</i>

168
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,733
<i>Mariela still needs to undergo</i>
<i>psychiatric evaluation.</i>

169
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:31,028
<i>And if proven that</i>
<i>she's mentally unfit, then…</i>

170
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:32,947
So what are you saying, Attorney?

171
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:36,450
So Bea still has a chance of
getting what she wants?

172
00:09:36,534 --> 00:09:40,162
<i>But the evaluation may take weeks.</i>
<i>Even months.</i>

173
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:43,291
- [CLICKS]
- [THUDS]

174
00:09:43,374 --> 00:09:48,921
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

175
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:53,050
Mariela Mercado.

176
00:09:57,305 --> 00:10:01,434
Miss, my mother doesn't need painkillers.

177
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:04,353
We cleaned her wound earlier, didn't we?

178
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:10,151
Yes, but I requested that, if possible,
she be transferred to a hospital.

179
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:12,903
We're already monitoring her condition.

180
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,156
That's not enough!

181
00:10:15,239 --> 00:10:18,618
Is my request that hard?!
My mother needs--

182
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:23,789
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:25,124
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

184
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:28,878
I'll take that.

185
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:31,797
[BEA] Thank you.

186
00:10:35,259 --> 00:10:36,677
So annoying.

187
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:37,887
Here, Ma.

188
00:10:40,097 --> 00:10:47,063
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

189
00:10:48,564 --> 00:10:51,776
Get some rest, Ma. Lie down first.

190
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:55,988
Go on.

191
00:11:05,289 --> 00:11:12,296
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

192
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:16,342
[BEA SIGHS DEEPLY]

193
00:11:31,565 --> 00:11:37,488
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

194
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:44,328
[JAIL CELL RATTLING]

195
00:11:45,579 --> 00:11:46,956
[SIGHS SHARPLY]

196
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:49,333
Tsk!

197
00:11:50,459 --> 00:11:51,919
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

198
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:55,131
<i>Is Papa not coming home?</i>
<i>Isn't he joining us?</i>

199
00:11:55,631 --> 00:12:00,344
<i>You're so dumb, aren't you?</i>

200
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:01,929
<i>You're stupid!</i>

201
00:12:02,721 --> 00:12:04,432
<i>You really take after your father.</i>

202
00:12:04,515 --> 00:12:06,475
<i>You're both useless!</i>

203
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:08,686
<i>Ma! Ma!</i>

204
00:12:08,769 --> 00:12:10,938
<i>- Take her.</i>
<i>- Ma.</i>

205
00:12:11,021 --> 00:12:13,649
<i>- Help her.</i>
<i>- Help! Ma.</i>

206
00:12:13,732 --> 00:12:16,068
<i>Ma, wake up! Ma!</i>

207
00:12:16,152 --> 00:12:18,404
[CRYING] <i>Ma!</i>

208
00:12:19,029 --> 00:12:20,489
[LABORED BREATHING]

209
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:22,783
<i>- Abigail!</i>
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

210
00:12:22,867 --> 00:12:25,202
<i>Abigail! Abigail!</i>

211
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:27,204
- [ABIGAIL BREATHING HEAVILY]
<i>- Abigail.</i>

212
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:28,831
<i>The question is,</i>

213
00:12:30,207 --> 00:12:33,169
<i>which one of us is the bigger thief?</i>

214
00:12:34,753 --> 00:12:35,963
<i>A thief?</i>

215
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:39,717
<i>What the hell are you talking about?</i>

216
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:43,387
<i>If only you knew.</i>

217
00:12:44,054 --> 00:12:45,890
<i>Knew what?</i>

218
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,978
<i>Why don't you just tell the truth,</i>

219
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:53,731
<i>so I can understand</i>
<i>where your anger is coming from?</i>

220
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:59,487
<i>What's your reason for going after me?</i>

221
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:03,282
<i>Ma.</i>

222
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:07,912
<i>No matter what happens,</i>

223
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:11,040
<i>don't tell them</i>

224
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:14,084
<i>that you know</i>
<i>they're Papa's second family.</i>

225
00:13:15,377 --> 00:13:16,420
<i>Why not?</i>

226
00:13:17,129 --> 00:13:18,339
<i>That's the truth.</i>

227
00:13:18,964 --> 00:13:20,424
<i>Ma.</i>

228
00:13:21,133 --> 00:13:22,927
<i>Please listen to me.</i>

229
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:32,102
[MUSIC BECOMES STIRRING]

230
00:13:39,276 --> 00:13:41,028
[BEA] <i>I was wrong, Ma.</i>

231
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:43,948
<i>The truth won't hurt us.</i>

232
00:13:45,783 --> 00:13:48,077
<i>It may even save us both.</i>

233
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:58,754
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

234
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:07,972
Attorney said Mariela
might get out of jail.

235
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:11,433
I can't let that happen, Auntie.

236
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,185
Of course.

237
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:16,438
Bea would do anything for her mother.

238
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:18,607
Just like you would for your father.

239
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:21,819
But that won't fix what happened.

240
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:29,118
Someone who is afraid to lose a loved one
is a tough opponent.

241
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:32,413
But fortunately, we are all safe.

242
00:14:32,496 --> 00:14:33,956
And so is your father.

243
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:37,126
Like I told Jordan,

244
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:41,255
what happened to us was devastating.

245
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:44,341
But when I found out

246
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:48,262
that Dad didn't forget about me,

247
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:54,435
everything we had lost
didn't seem to matter anymore.

248
00:14:56,061 --> 00:14:58,689
Because Dad came back to us.

249
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:06,238
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

250
00:15:13,495 --> 00:15:16,248
AMIHAN HOME

251
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:24,340
[TENDER MUSIC PLAYING]

252
00:15:32,556 --> 00:15:34,475
Is there a problem, Jordan?

253
00:15:35,726 --> 00:15:37,603
- Grandpa?
- Did you get into a fight?

254
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:41,690
No, Grandpa.

255
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:47,237
There's just so much going on with Billy.

256
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:51,158
Her house burned down.

257
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:55,955
And LoveList is having problems
with investors.

258
00:15:57,581 --> 00:16:01,210
But it's good that she and her father
have made amends.

259
00:16:02,461 --> 00:16:04,755
You and your father are okay now?

260
00:16:04,838 --> 00:16:06,173
Has he gotten his act together?

261
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:09,635
No, I'm talking about
Billy and her father.

262
00:16:09,718 --> 00:16:10,719
- Not…
- [JUDE] Huh?

263
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:12,596
Never mind.

264
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:17,643
[HUFFS]

265
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:28,779
She's such a fighter, Grandpa.

266
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,825
Despite everything,

267
00:16:34,535 --> 00:16:38,414
she's always there
for the people who need her.

268
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:40,833
[MOVING MUSIC PLAYING]

269
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:42,710
Even if it isn't easy…

270
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:47,256
Even though I know that
it could ruin our friendship…

271
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:52,553
I can't help it.

272
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:59,059
I'm falling in love with her.

273
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:03,772
["THE PUZZLE" BY
BELLE MARIANO PLAYING]

274
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:05,315
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

275
00:17:12,489 --> 00:17:14,408
Thank you for listening.

276
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:21,415
["THE PUZZLE" CONTINUES]

277
00:17:22,666 --> 00:17:25,377
[JAIL CELL CREAKS OPEN]

278
00:17:25,461 --> 00:17:27,796
- [INMATE 1] Sir, good evening.
- [JAIL GUARD] Go to sleep.

279
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,798
- [INMATE 2] Good night, sir.
- [JAIL GUARD] Okay.

280
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:32,092
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]
- Enough chitchat. Go to sleep!

281
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:34,386
- [BATON TAPS JAIL CELL]
- [DINO] We will be blessed

282
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:37,473
if we just trust His word and
dedicate our lives to Him.

283
00:17:37,556 --> 00:17:40,059
- [JAIL CELL CLANGS]
- After you pray, go to sleep.

284
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:41,435
Yes, sir.

285
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,188
- [JAIL GUARD] Hit the sack!
- [INMATE 3] Yes, sir.

286
00:17:44,271 --> 00:17:49,234
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

287
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:51,570
Is everything ready for Family Day?

288
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:54,531
Boss.

289
00:17:55,407 --> 00:17:57,284
We can no longer use
the garbage holding area.

290
00:17:58,202 --> 00:18:00,370
We checked last night.
The railings were replaced.

291
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:08,879
[MUSIC BECOMES TENSE]

292
00:18:17,137 --> 00:18:18,222
[MUSIC FADES]

293
00:18:18,305 --> 00:18:19,431
Attorney.

294
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:23,185
I can request to speak to Billy, right?

295
00:18:24,728 --> 00:18:27,773
I can just relay your message to her.

296
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:29,775
No.

297
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:33,278
I have to tell her myself.
We need to talk in person.

298
00:18:34,446 --> 00:18:37,950
Well, we can make a request.

299
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:40,994
But there's no guarantee
that she'll agree.

300
00:18:41,745 --> 00:18:44,665
And besides, I'm your lawyer.

301
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:48,877
Anything you intend to say to her
should go through me first.

302
00:18:49,878 --> 00:18:53,507
I know that.
But this is a personal matter.

303
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:57,970
So I want to talk to her alone
and tell her myself.

304
00:18:59,096 --> 00:19:00,681
Whatever it is,

305
00:19:01,431 --> 00:19:02,933
it's better if I know.

306
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:06,436
Because it might aggravate your case

307
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:08,981
even if you have good intentions.

308
00:19:10,941 --> 00:19:13,110
What is it that you want
to say to Ms. Cariño?

309
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:17,573
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

310
00:19:17,656 --> 00:19:18,699
Attorney.

311
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:21,076
Please submit a request

312
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:24,413
so I can personally talk to Billy.

313
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:36,091
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

314
00:19:58,989 --> 00:20:02,284
<i>We need to find</i>
<i>potential investors!</i>

315
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:03,785
<i>If not Claire, who?</i>

316
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,287
<i>If not the US,</i>
<i>then where?!</i>

317
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:07,039
[ENRICO]
<i>I just don't know how to say it</i>

318
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:09,708
<i>because I don't want to</i>
<i>hurt you again.</i>

319
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:11,168
<i>What is it?</i>

320
00:20:13,754 --> 00:20:15,672
<i>Strong coffee</i>
<i>for a strong woman.</i>

321
00:20:16,715 --> 00:20:18,300
<i>I don't think this is enough.</i>

322
00:20:18,383 --> 00:20:20,385
<i>We're going to stay up</i>
<i>all night at work.</i>

323
00:20:20,469 --> 00:20:22,846
<i>I disappointed our chief again.</i>

324
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:25,182
<i>Hey, don't take it to heart.</i>
<i>It's just work.</i>

325
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:26,558
<i>Mm-hmm.</i>

326
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:31,563
<i>You're one to talk. I saw how negative</i>
<i>your vibe became earlier.</i>

327
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:34,399
<i>Bea asked to speak</i>
<i>with you in person.</i>

328
00:20:34,483 --> 00:20:36,985
<i>Can't she just say whatever it is</i>
<i>through her lawyer?</i>

329
00:20:37,069 --> 00:20:38,862
[Granado] <i>Bea's adamant.</i>

330
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:41,281
<i>She insists it's a… family matter?</i>

331
00:20:41,949 --> 00:20:44,743
<i>I don't have all day.</i>
<i>I'm a busy person.</i>

332
00:20:44,826 --> 00:20:46,036
<i>Billy, sorry.</i>

333
00:20:46,787 --> 00:20:50,624
<i>Have you run out of tricks</i>
<i>to escape from this?</i>

334
00:20:50,707 --> 00:20:54,628
<i>Your apology won't erase</i>
<i>all the harm you've done to my family.</i>

335
00:20:54,711 --> 00:20:56,004
<i>I wronged you.</i>

336
00:20:56,088 --> 00:20:57,798
<i>I wronged your family too.</i>

337
00:20:57,881 --> 00:21:00,425
<i>- I did it because you stole from me.</i>
<i>- I never stole anything from you.</i>
